%I A400569 #13 Oct 08 2026 18:52:44
%S A400569 1,1,3,14,101,1495,102268
%N A400569 Number of nonisomorphic commutative dimonoids of order n.
%C A400569 A dimonoid is an algebraic structure (D,-|,|-) consisting of a set D equipped with two associative binary operations -| and |- satisfying the following axioms:
%C A400569   (x -| y) -| z = x -| (y |- z),
%C A400569   (x |- y) -| z = x |- (y -| z),
%C A400569   (x -| y) |- z = x |- (y |- z).
%C A400569 A dimonoid (D,-|,|-) is called commutative if both (D,-|) and D,|-) are commutative semigroups.
%H A400569 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1080/00927872.2026.2712633">On dimonoids of small order</a>, Commun. Algebra, 1-15 (2026).
%H A400569 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2607.17921">On dimonoids of small order</a>, arXiv:2607.17921 [math.GR], 2026.
%H A400569 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22646186">Lists of All Pairwise Nonisomorphic Commutative Dimonoids of Orders up to 6</a>, Zenodo, 2026.
%H A400569 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://gist.github.com/vgavrylkiv/b41c66cce83a13e008168d06e0b6988d">Python code for computing nonisomorphic dimonoids</a>.
%e A400569 For n = 2, there are exactly 3 pairwise nonisomorphic commutative dimonoids (D,-|,|-) on the set D={0,1}. Rows and columns are ordered as 0,1. The Cayley tables of all three dimonoids are listed below.
%e A400569 Dimonoid #1:
%e A400569   -|:   |-:
%e A400569   0 0   0 0
%e A400569   0 0   0 0
%e A400569 Dimonoid #2:
%e A400569   -|:   |-:
%e A400569   0 1   0 1
%e A400569   1 0   1 0
%e A400569 Dimonoid #3:
%e A400569   -|:   |-:
%e A400569   0 0   0 0
%e A400569   0 1   0 1
%Y A400569 Cf. A027851, A001426, A400568, A400570.
%K A400569 nonn,more,new
%O A400569 0,3
%A A400569 _Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv_, Sep 30 2026
